  "instance_name": "childhood_innocence_as_mask",
  "label": "Use of Childhood Innocence as a Mask for Racism",
  "description": "The meme leverages the perceived innocence of childhood to disguise a racist message. By stating 'when ur too young to know racism', it implies that the children's happiness is pure and uncorrupted, thereby making the racist framing seem more acceptable or less offensive. This requires understanding how societal norms and media often use childhood innocence as a rhetorical device to soften or justify harmful ideologies.",
